.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-VOLUME 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-volume
.Nd the Patina desktop's volume menu
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -flash | -brightness
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the volume menu in the bar's tray: a mute button, a slider and the
level, at the bar's right end.
It stays until Escape, a click elsewhere, or the speaker again.
.Pp
It also flashes up after a volume or brightness key: it fades in without
taking the keyboard, shows what the key changed, holds while the keys keep
coming, and fades out on its own.
The keys themselves are handled by
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
which runs its
.Ic [media]
commands and then
.Nm
with
.Fl -flash
or
.Fl -brightness ;
.Nm
only shows the result.
.Pp
Only one runs at a time.
Running it while one is open passes the request on: a second plain run
closes the menu, and a flash keeps an open one up or restarts its hold.
.Pp
The volume is the default output's, read and set with
.Xr wpctl 1 ;
the brightness is the backlight's.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -flash
Show the volume briefly, without taking the keyboard.
.It Fl -brightness
Show the screen's brightness briefly.
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATINA_SKIN
The skin to wear, as the bar sets it; otherwise the bar's config's.
.It Ev PATINA_BAR_EDGE
.Dq top
or
.Dq bottom :
which edge to open from.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-bar 1 ,
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr wpctl 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
